From: Noswad <64293615+TheNoswad@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: gs101-oriole: add fuel gauge battery models

Expose the battery-ID byte of the pack EEPROM (offset 0x17: 2 = COS,
3 = LSN, as in Google's google_eeprom.c) as an nvmem cell for the fuel
gauge, and add the oriole models from Google's
gs101-oriole-battery-data.dtsi so the gauge gets the right model after
a power-on reset. Verified on a LSN pack (ID 3).
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101-oriole-battery.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101-oriole-battery.dtsi
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f4926e3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs101-oriole-battery.dtsi
@@ -0,0 +1,135 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+/*
+ * Oriole battery models for the MAX77759 fuel gauge, from the Google
+ * gs101-oriole-battery-data.dtsi (raviole kernel CP2A.260705.006).
+ *
+ * Copyright 2020 Google LLC
+ */
+
+&fuel_gauge {
+	/* 06_p1_gen.ini, 2021-01-05, b/174788070, generic model */
+	model-generic {
+		maxim,battery-id = <0>;
+		maxim,fg-model = /bits/ 16 <
+			0x9760 0xa510 0xb100 0xb600 0xb7a0 0xb900 0xba70 0xbc70
